{
    "schema": "blocks-engine/php-transformer/parity-fixture/v1",
    "name": "html-nav-toggle-class-union",
    "description": "A separate desktop nav (base display:none, flex at a breakpoint) and a separate mobile toggle button (visible at rest, hidden at that same breakpoint, with its own box-sizing utilities) must not have their class lists unioned onto one core/navigation. The toggle's own visibility/sizing classes describe the control the nav's overlayMenu already represents, not the navigation container itself; unioning them produces a self-contradictory className (both 'hidden'/'md:flex' and 'md:hidden' on the same element) and pins the toggle's small fixed box size onto the nav at every breakpoint.",
    "source_reference": {
        "repo": "php-transformer",
        "path": "tests/fixtures/parity/html-nav-toggle-class-union.json",
        "notes": "Regression fixture for fix/nav-toggle-class-union. Reduced from a real capture where a `hidden md:flex` <nav> and a sibling `md:hidden` hamburger <button> (3 SVG lines, no aria-controls/aria-label) were merged into one core/navigation whose className carried both opposing responsive-visibility classes plus the button's w-9/h-9 box size."
    },
